545f-ac10-98880196af2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71798" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- $(-\\infty ,-2)$\n- $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$\n- $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-\\infty ,-2)$ is open. The boundary point of the set is $-2$ and it does not lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$ has four boundary points $0$, $2$, $7$, and $9$, and the points $2$, $7$, and $9$ lies in the set.\n\n- $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$ has four boundary points $-5$, $-1$, $2$, and $4$, and the points $-5$ and $-1$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71798/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71798"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71802/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "05b22d51-c74e-5f14-9f29-36f41d10547e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71802/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "39caf4b2-4d44-51b6-a917-ec27da388cfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71802/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "00528e60-ed33-5124-a712-3fc52ce3013c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {