s *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(2,5)$ and $(-3,0)\\cup (2,7)$ are open because:\n\n- The boundary points of the set $(2,5)$ are $2$, and $5.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of the set  $(-3,0)\\cup (2,7)$ are $-3$, $0$, $2$, and $7.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not open because $(-2,2)\\cup (4,10]$ has four boundary points $-2$, $2$, $4$, and $10$, and the point $10$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105201/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105201"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71791/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "173d05e7-01f8-51b4-a99e-999eb2297643" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71791/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "bda3ac34-c1f5-5c5b-9aa0-f0172157000f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71791/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3b2fa85d-6a95-50ac-97d9-aec3ea556a7a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71791/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "b8dbffa8-6113-59da-ad39-c2488257d668" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III onl