+2{y}^{2}\\le 3}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1<x<1,\\,0<y<2-{x}^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161638/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105437/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "55c7ce74-344d-5b69-a062-90cbe219484e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105437/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "6e2f51fb-2346-52bd-9e2c-6e112ce40eee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105437/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ec164832-e720-548e-991e-8ff1af22f197" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105437/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" 