er is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71820/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71820"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105431/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "29f023d2-2064-5cdc-a5ef-c058e30d6f91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105431/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ef53dfc8-200c-5474-b7e1-c64b5a1d82fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105431/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cff2b96b-dbed-5280-9268-b4aadcd1deba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105431/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "35b76b0f-46cf-5b09-971f-900e6e0dd695" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105431/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "b5eaa4f2-1716-59e3-8fea-3c8121d21566" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105431/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae6c39a-b585-5e84-b961-eddb4396d8ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105431/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-105431/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-105431/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-105431/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-105431/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-105431/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105431" :question/id #uuid "515e62a9-8010-5981-a943-f92eefe22e5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105431" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 6,\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 3}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}<9,\\,1<{y}^{2}<16}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2},\\,-2\\le x\\le 2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,\\sqrt{3}).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105431/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105431"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71815/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ba642d60-01ad-5d63-a3a9-d8b681b